<title>GERMANY: Bonn issues 8.568bln dmk Bubills at 98.53 and over.</title>
<headline>Bonn issues 8.568bln dmk Bubills at 98.53 and over.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German government on Wednesday issued 8.568 billion marks of six-month Treasury Bills, or Bubills, at an auction at a lowest accepted price of 98.525, the Bundesbank as issuing agent said.</p>
<p>The weighted average price was 98.528 and the average yield was 2.96 percent, the Bundesbank said.</p>
<p>Bids for the paper totalled 20.31 billion marks, the Bundesbank said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
